--
-- A node is a state with a view: stopped, sending (the message and the state after), receiving
-- (the state after each answer), reading the clock, or taking a silent step. A process over
-- NetSig M is a node (its tree of steps is the state, proc-view), a guarded process at every
-- clock is one (gview), and a machine with a first-order state is one directly. A fleet is the
-- nodes' behaviour by node id (Beh) and a global state: every node's state and the network.
-- One step is one choice of the adversary, resolved by lib/net.cub and answered by net-world.
-- fleet-run folds a recorded list of choices; fleet-at follows an infinite sequence.
--
-- Property types (their inhabitants are proofs): Safe, Live, Refines, Converges, and replay.
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------- nodes and the global state
import "net.hypercubical"
